  "body": "Unit complex query phases and any number of unit root rotations cannot reduce PR944/PR1088's fixed three-by-three dirty connector below **14 complete child queries**. With positive fixed complete operator tariffs, the optimum remains `2 sum_F c_F + 2 min_F c_F`.\n\n**Status: scoped negative result; no new kappa.** Concurrent #1551 establishes the finite sixth-root case. This contribution adds the entire complex unit circle and arbitrary unit root rotations, using support-graph normalization and a geometric collapse of a three-step triangle to the older signed obstruction. Its finite sixth-root census is independent corroboration; no priority over #1551 is claimed. That PR and Discussion #1539 were found during the final overlap follow-up and their exact proof scope was inspected before submission.\n\nThe written argument only needs the existing 720-path signed exclusion. Additional exact evidence covers all 30,240 normalized triangle paths and checks every collapse with a separate implementation. A thirteen-query control succeeds when a coefficient of magnitude two is admitted, while a five-query unit-phase fixture verifies that odd restored words are legal. These controls separate the new restriction from signed parity and unrestricted scalar coefficients.\n\nOnly `research/complex-unit-phase-connector-seed39/` is added. It contains the proof, certificate, source pins, local claim, overlap record, two implementations, complete factor-cost recurrence and explicit replay hook.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/complex-unit-phase-connector-seed39\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/complex-unit-phase-connector-seed39 outcome=negative-result`.\n\nLocal checks passed:\n\n- Registered Python 3.12.13 replay, including optimized execution, source bindings and both exact implementations.\n- 1,728 attaining orbit words, 18 root-gauged words, 172 semantic controls, six complete arbitrary-dirty factor expansions and 444 dense forward/inverse pairs with noncommuting maps.\n- Read-only relocation, deterministic regeneration and six on-disk source/certificate rejection controls.\n- Normal Python 3.14 direct checks, all 20 research-onboarding tests, selected-record integrity and whitespace checks.\n\nBase: `ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6`; OS assignment seed 39, complex-supplier track. Refreshed main `c5108f0f68d482e5712a8e26a5978d47762dfc16` leaves all live inputs and the selected result unchanged; its ledger changes are historical provenance only. The late #1551 comparison is pinned at `be8768d5fd8e9e7a1f714424f25b34b0e807daa0`.\n\nNo selected-supplier instance, native hosting, rounded precision, physical runtime saving, selected cold replay, proof-assistant theorem or independent human review is claimed. The result requires exact complex-linear maps, immutable sources, one dirty root and the stated query alphabet. No merge or frontier promotion is requested.\n\nCredit Ross Richardson / #944 and @martinxxx9 / #1088 for the signed obstruction and six attaining repairs; concurrent #1551 for the sixth-root result, #1526 for paid magnitude scaling, and #1349 for the F3 comparison. Prepared by **Hanson Sun (@bbMisk)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance** in reasoning, implementation, verification and prose. Apache-2.0.\n",
